finitely on the same lock, hanging shutdown.\n\n- candidate_36 only renames/refactors `submitUserTask` and tightens exception handling in\n  `fireDisconnect()`; it does not touch the `synchronized` modifier on `exit()`.\n\n- The state right before the fix (matching the `57ef52d` blob hash referenced in\n  fix_commit_diff.txt) still has `private volatile boolean connected;` and\n  `public synchronized void exit()`, i.e., exactly what candidate_35 produced, carried\n  forward unchanged by candidate_36.\n\nSince the fix is specifically about removing the naive `synchronized` locking on `exit()`\nin favor of atomic/CAS-based coordination, candidate_35 is the commit that introduced the\nprecise faulty synchronization strategy being corrected. (candidate_24, which introduced\nthe `connected` field and the exit-calls-itself pattern, is a contributing/related change,\nbut the actual defect targeted by this fix \u2014 synchronizing `exit()` \u2014 was introduced in\ncandidate_35.)\n"
